ana  a few laughs  we're going to try  vanessa murphy live local now the  solution if you're interested in  learning more about this we do have a  link over at 8newsnow.com martinez says  volunteers do have to go through  background checks there's a vetting  process and training before taking part  also in the school district see three  ccsd board seats are up for grabs this  year trustee president irene cepeda has  already filed to run again danielle  ford's seat is also up for re-election  and so is her board rival linda cavazos  however neither of them have filed to  run again just yet  next on politics now finding affordable  housing  what can be done today to try and at  least make this the smallest of dents in  the crisis of affordable housing  vouchers vouchers vouchers  vouchers coming up we will break down  what affordable housing means why we  have so little of it and possible  solutions from the local  vegas strong walker furniture  you're watching politics now  with home prices and rents at record  levels there's a push in nevada for more  affordable housing so we have some  questions first what is affordable  housing well clark county and nevada  essentially define it as housing where  the person living in the home is paying  no more than 30 percent of their gross  income for housing costs that would  include utilities now for a person who  makes about 40 000 a year that would be  a thousand dollars per month for rent  and utilities here in clark county there  are 17 thousand just a little more than  that seventeen thousand rental units  that meet the definition right now of  affordable housing another seventeen  hundred more than that or so are uh  already under in progress so seventeen  thousand existing seventeen hundred in  progress is this enough well no i spoke  with audra hammernick with nevada hand  it's a nonprofit dedicated to creating  affordable housing we spoke about this  issue  what is the need right now  so the need right now the number 