le housing  sometimes it works really well and  sometimes it doesn't it's very expensive  to build  bathrooms and kitchens and that's what  ends up being apartment units so it's  possible and um some of those things um  take a long time too just because it's a  zoning use change in the same way that  we might need that on the new  construction side the second thing that  i mentioned is we're really  happy and proud about the southern  nevada regional housing authority their  board of commissioners hired a stand-up  new executive director  he's his name's louis jordan he's  talking publicly about creating a  project-based section 8 program and that  is the other thing that could really  help move the needle on affordable  housing because adding that voucher  component to buildings gives people more  purchase power in the rental market  we're also working with senator cortez  masto's office  to get just more vouchers into nevada  when you look at some of the  eastern cities that had higher  populations that are losing folks and  then you look at nevada when we're  deeply growing  the hud formula just simply is not fair  it's saying that  what you got last year vouchers is what  you're going to get now and it's it's  there's an inequity there and we're  going to really try hard to get more of  those vouchers can las vegas ever  actually  catch up to what is needed for  affordable housing  well john i live in hope  i think that  it's going to be rough because we have  some really big numbers right 84 000  units is a lot of units  but the  american rescue plan act dollars that  are funds that are coming in the state  has dedicated 500 million for affordable  housing  300 plus  million just on the multi-family side  which is great the county has dedicated  150 million  pair those with 9 tax credits and you  can build a lot of units is it going to  get you 84 000 not even close  hammer nick says it takes about 18  months for a new affordable housing unit  to come online  t